<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>fabric-selections</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/cut-and-sew.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/polos.css">
</head>

<body>
     <%- include('partials/nav') %>
    <section class="hero-section">
        <div class="hero-bg-container">
            <img src="../photos/fabric-selections.jpg" alt="Vito and Will folded polo shirts" class="hero-image">
        </div>

    </section>
    <section class="manufacturing-services">
        <div class="container">
            <h2 class="section-title">Fabric Selection for Custom Clothing</h2>

            <p class="section-text">
                Fabric selection is one of the most crucial steps in designing any apparel line. While 100% cotton and
                100% polyester are the most common choices, there are many other fabric types to explore—each offering
                unique qualities for different garments.




            </p>

            <p class="section-text">
                At Fabuluxe Industry, we provide a wide range of fabrics suitable for casual wear, sportswear, premium
                collections, and more, along with full customization to meet your brand’s vision.




            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="services-section">
        <div class="container">

            <div class="service-row">
                <div class="service-image">
                    <img src="../photos/fabric-selections1.jpg" alt="Close up of hands using a sewing machine">
                </div>
                <div class="service-content">
                    <h2 class="service-title">Casual Jersey Fabrics</h2>
                    <p class="service-text">
                        Casual jersey fabrics are knitted fabrics that are lightweight, breathable, and versatile. We
                        offer single jersey, interlock jersey, double jersey, and jacquard jersey options—perfect for
                        T-shirts, women’s tops, shorts, pocket tees, and other everyday wear. You can choose 100%
                        cotton, 100% polyester, or blended fabrics such as 60% cotton and 40% polyester. For bulk
                        orders, we can also customize jersey fabrics to your exact requirements.



                    </p>

                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="service-row row-reverse">
                <div class="service-image">
                    <img src="../photos/fabric-selections3.jpg" alt="Tailor working with denim fabric at a workbench">
                </div>
                <div class="service-content">
                    <h2 class="service-title">Fleece Fabrics</h2>
                    <p class="service-text">
                        Fleece is a thicker fabric, commonly used for hoodies, sweatshirts, and sweaters. We offer
                        fleece in different weights (grams per square meter), allowing you to decide the garment’s
                        heaviness depending on the season or target market. For a lighter alternative, French Terry
                        fabric is also available—ideal for cozy yet breathable apparel.






                    </p>


                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="dye-services-section">
        <div class="container">

            <div class="dye-row">
                <div class="dye-image">
                    <img src="../photos/fabric-selections33.jpg" alt="Colorful sublimated and dyed athletic t-shirts">
                </div>
                <div class="dye-content">
                    <h2 class="dye-title">Sports Fabrics</h2>
                    <p class="dye-text">
                        Sportswear demands durability, flexibility, and comfort. We supply specialized fabrics like
                        nylon spandex, polyester spandex, and cotton spandex—perfect for basketball jerseys, leggings,
                        yoga pants, and fitted T-shirts. If you require something more specific, we can customize sports
                        fabrics to match your performance and design needs.



                    </p>

                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="dye-row row-reverse">
                <div class="dye-image">
                    <img src="../photos/fabric-selections4.jpg"
                        alt="A collection of vibrant fabric color swatches arranged together">
                </div>
                <div class="dye-content">
                    <h2 class="dye-title">Premium Fabrics</h2>
                    <p class="dye-text">
                        To elevate your designs, we also provide premium fabrics such as silk, satin, woven cotton, and
                        both artificial and real leather. These fabrics add sophistication and exclusivity to garments,
                        whether used for full pieces or as details like sleeves, trims, or patches. Premium fabrics give
                        designers the freedom to experiment and create standout apparel.



                    </p>

                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>
    <section>
        <div class="container">
            <div class="service-row">
                <div class="service-image">
                    <img src="../photos/fabric-selections5.jpg" alt="Close up of hands using a sewing machine">
                </div>
                <div class="service-content">
                    <h2 class="service-title">Hosiery Fabrics</h2>
                    <p class="service-text">
                        Hosiery fabrics are stretchy and soft, commonly used for leggings, tights, and undergarments.
                        However, their versatility allows them to be used for lightweight, stretchable T-shirts and
                        other creative apparel pieces. Our customization options enable you to combine hosiery with
                        other fabrics for unique results.


                    </p>
                   
                    <a href="#" class="trigger-popup-btn btn-quote">Get a Qoute</a>
                </div>
            </div>
    </section>6


<%- include('partials/popup') %>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>

</body>

</html>
